# Owner-employee payroll

## Pay runs (Supabase `payroll_runs`)

- Link each run to an `employee` record.
- Separate **employee withholdings** (income tax, RPC, AE, RQAP) from **employer contributions**.
- Net pay = gross − employee withholdings − other deductions, **plus** non-taxable reimbursements (TTC) and GST/QST on taxable reimbursements.
- Taxable employee expenses: HT added to gross (pensionable); employee still receives full TTC.
- Estimates use **2026** Québec rates (QPP 6.3% + QPP2 4%, AE Québec 1.30% unless **>40% voting shares**, RQAP 0.430%/0.602%, abattement fédéral 16,5 %, FSS on salary with no 40% exclusion). Draft for CPA review — not a payroll provider.
- **EI / AE**: skip employee and employer premiums when the employee has more than 40% of voting shares (flag or cap table). RQAP, QPP, and HSF/FSS still apply to that salary.

## Remittances

- Track source deductions remitted to Revenu Québec / CRA outside the app (bank confirmations).
- Employer portions (RPC, AE, RQAP employeur) are additional cash outflows.

## Salary vs dividends

- Salary: payroll module with statutory deductions.
- Dividends: `dividends` table with equal split among active employees by default.
- Present trade-offs; owner confirms mix with CPA.

## Year-end

- Draft T4/RL-1 summaries from `payroll_runs` — CPA files.
